{"c":[{"id":"ff4a86710809ce02","sum":"Dead shim: ENOENT/ENOTDIR/ELOOP; EACCES/ESTALE stay. Owner: claude if installed_plugins.json beside cache/ lists the root, cursor via CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT, else ask. Local-path mkts load from source. orphan=version-dir+.orphaned_at. CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/..._CACHE_DIR move plugins.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"c1e11d92dfb9eca2","sum":"ENOENT/ENOTDIR/ELOOP=dead;EACCES/ESTALE stay. Claude ask; Cursor=CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT. installed_plugins.json beside cache/=cache copy not checkout; dir-mkt. --plugin-dir/synced none. orphan=version-dir+.orphaned_at. CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR+CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_CACHE_DIR move plugins root.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"fea602b5005e86e1","sum":"shim _alive is dead only on ENOENT/ENOTDIR/ELOOP. EACCES/ESTALE stay alive, so rectify leaves it. Path.is_file raises before 3.14 and returns False from 3.14. Claude-only fixes must not question Cursor users. sr-initialize asks only in Claude Code; Cursor uses CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261016T215531Z-cabd5aa56838fc34","text":"shim _alive: only ENOENT/ENOTDIR/ELOOP mean a baked engine is dead; other stat errors (EACCES, ESTALE) count as alive, so rectify leaves it. Do not use Path.is_file: it raises those before Python 3.14 and returns False from 3.14.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261016T222048Z-5c4cd091dd70b15f","text":"Design rule (operator, 2026-10-16): fixes for Claude Code-only problems must not add questions for Cursor users. sr-initialize asks the user only in Claude Code; Cursor keeps its own evidence (CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"dc126cfe9aa69545","sum":"installed_plugins.json beside cache/ lists only the cache copy, never the checkout (dir-marketplace too). --plugin-dir and synced copies: none; orphans keep version-dir plus .orphaned_at. Cursor: no record. CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR and CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_CACHE_DIR move the plugins root.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261016T223043Z-086a0d75fd95fd94","text":"Claude Code proves an install by its record, not its folder: installed_plugins.json in the plugins root (beside cache/) lists each installPath; --plugin-dir (@inline) and synced copies have none; orphans keep a version-named folder plus .orphaned_at. Cursor has no such record.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261017T010120Z-43ea3096fec682fc","text":"Claude Code copies even directory-marketplace plugins (source ./ too) into <plugins root>/cache/<mkt>/<plugin>/<version>; installed_plugins.json there records only that copy, never the checkout. CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR and CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_CACHE_DIR both move the plugins root.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ea3fa59ce852af66","sum":"Owner outside default plugin dirs: claude if installed_plugins.json beside cache/ lists the exact root (before CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT), else none. Local-path marketplaces load from source, not installPath. ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA}=<plugins root>/data/<id>; read paths via quoted heredoc.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"0759e81a67d39207","sum":"Outside default plugin folders, claude means installed_plugins.json beside cache/ lists the exact plugin root (before CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT); else no owner. A local-path marketplace caches and records a relative-path plugin, but loads it from the source folder, not installPath.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261017T012636Z-cb621eb5522291ae","text":"sr-initialize Step 2: an install-shaped copy outside the default plugins folders is claude when installed_plugins.json beside its cache/ holds the quoted exact plugin root (grep -qF), checked before CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT; else no owner. Supersedes the round-1 owner-rule note.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261017T014809Z-c4ddf9bb24e2c594","text":"Correction: relative-path plugins in a local-path Claude Code marketplace get a cache entry and an install record, but load in place from the source folder (claude plugin list --json readFromFolder). installPath is not always the folder a plugin loads from.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"477b2af74f8da1f7","sum":"CC 2.1.302 substitutes ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA} in skill text: <plugins root>/data/<id>, id stockroom-inline (--plugin-dir) or stockroom-<marketplace>; 'inline' reserved. SKILL_DIR=\"${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}\" re-parses the pasted path; quoted-heredoc IFS= read -r is safe.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261017T135741Z-0a0d4ec0ff68165a","text":"Claude Code 2.1.302 substitutes ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA} in plugin skill text (typed or model-invoked, prose or fence): <plugins root>/data/<id>, id stockroom-inline for --plugin-dir, stockroom-<marketplace> for installs. Marketplace name 'inline' is reserved.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261017T135751Z-db7b381ea6596dc0","text":"sr-initialize Step 2: SKILL_DIR=\"${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}\" lets the shell re-parse the pasted path ($x, backtick, $(), quote pairs change it or run commands; a lone \" is a syntax error). A quoted-heredoc IFS= read -r passed all cases in dash/bash/busybox.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"8f544ca9fb1ae138","sum":"Hooks expand ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}; Step 2 reads pasted paths via quoted heredoc; owner rules in systemPatterns. Shell and printed paths quoted. Cron/launchd carry PATH+STOCKROOM_HOME. Git-archive engine copy: git init+add -A for reuse lint. Torch fail: ensure-env if freeze.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"3ce3ee33dcc4f281","sum":"Hooks expand \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}\" from env; skill text is pasted raw, so Step 2 reads paths via quoted heredoc. Owner: claude if <root>/data/<id> or installed_plugins.json lists it, dev if stockroom-inline, cursor via CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT, else ask. Shell paths quoted.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"def92aca321a0958","sum":"CC 2.1.302 hooks expand \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}\" from env (safe); skill text is pasted raw. sr-initialize owner: default plugin dirs by path; else claude if <copy root>/data/<id> or installed_plugins.json lists it, dev if stockroom-inline, cursor via CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT, else ask.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261017T135752Z-8f76ec9421650d2c","text":"Claude Code 2.1.302 shell-form hooks: \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}\" is expanded by the shell from the env, not pasted as text (a $ in the path survives), so hooks/claude-hooks.json is safe from path re-parsing. Skill text is pasted raw.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261017T143558Z-05746a642d0f531d","text":"sr-initialize Step 2 owner (round 3): default plugins dirs by path; elsewhere a cache-shaped copy is claude if Claude's data dir is <copy root>/data/<id> or installed_plugins.json lists it, dev if data dir is stockroom-inline, cursor via CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT, else ask.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ed3458896fa1f4ac","sum":"sr-initialize Step 2 reads ${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA} from a quoted heredoc (IFS= read -r); a value still starting with $ was not substituted. Paths in shell text are quoted (shlex.quote, Makefile \"...\"): space and ' work; $, backtick, \", \\, % out of scope.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261017T143616Z-2bbea48021b44381","text":"sr-initialize Step 2 now reads ${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR} and ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA} from a quoted heredoc (IFS= read -r), so the shell never parses the pasted paths and no env var stands in; a value still starting with $ was not substituted. Supersedes the SKILL_DIR=\"...\" note.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261018T171632Z-1ff8e252c90ac5da","text":"Every path stockroom writes into shell text is quoted: Step 2 heredoc, shim and scheduler entries via shlex.quote, Makefile recipes via double quotes. A space or ' must work; rarer chars ($, backtick, \", \\, %) are out of scope (2026-10-18).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f2b8fe2f4481d376","sum":"Nightly cron/launchd entries carry PATH and STOCKROOM_HOME; schedule status shows up-to-date and entry home; Step 8 offers re-install. Printed commands quote paths too. A git-archive engine copy needs git init + add -A for reuse lint. Torch fail: ensure-env if freeze, else pip.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"6b46287778b27850","sum":"Nightly cron/launchd entries carry PATH and STOCKROOM_HOME (no profile); 'schedule status' shows up-to-date: and entry home:, and Step 8 offers re-install. Path quoting covers printed commands too (doctor smoke remedy, localdev hint): audit messages, not only shell code.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261018T171639Z-5cb80849a2e584b6","text":"Nightly cron/launchd entries carry PATH and the resolved STOCKROOM_HOME (no shell profile is loaded); 'schedule status' prints up-to-date: and entry home:, and sr-initialize Step 8 offers a consented re-install of a stale entry.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261018T203924Z-9f05cc054dcdf6ff","text":"Path quoting also covers commands stockroom prints for someone to run (doctor smoke's torch remedy, localdev.sh's --plugin-dir hint). When auditing shell text, search printed messages too, not only code that runs a shell.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"8039db218a133a07","sum":"Engine suite from a git-archive copy: test_reuse_lint_passes fails once coverage-engine's sync made the copy's .venv; git init + git add -A avoids it. semantic/embed exit 1 with one torch line: ensure-env if a usable freeze exists, else the quoted pip line.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261018T211547Z-7e6ede0556b999df","text":"Engine suite from a git-archive copy (empty .git marker): test_reuse_lint_passes fails whenever make coverage-engine's sync has created the copy's skills/sr-search/.venv first; git init plus git add -A in the copy avoids it.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261020T175250Z-aa5758b35ed49d8e","text":"semantic and embed exit 1 with one torch line: ensure-env when a usable freeze exists, else the quoted pip line; an encoder failure after import says re-run sr-initialize, not ensure-env.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
